- [ ] A workout GPS file that arrives in a later sync than its summary is ACKed and its route dropped #workouts #worth(yes) #where(My Band/BLE/BandSyncer.swift:496) #added(2026-11-02)
	> @anchor: } else if meta.isWorkoutGps {
	> The track goes into workoutRoutes, but writeWorkouts runs only when the same batch
	> has a parsed summary (BandSyncer.swift:645), and nothing attaches a route to a
	> workout already in Health. The GPS file is ACKed anyway, so the band never offers it
	> again and the route is lost for good. The comment at the ACK names this case but
	> fixes only the ACK. Fix: attach an unmatched track to the app's own workout in Health
	> by start time (HKWorkoutRouteBuilder on the existing HKWorkout), or leave the file
	> un-ACKed until its summary is written. Found while investigating the 2026-11-01 walk,
	> which hit a different bug.
